SRC/hexedit -- changes made for the OSK freeware collection  Rebuilt 2026-09-26 with Microware's cc against LIB/ncurses.l, with  moria's tcentry.c (SRC/moria) linked ahead of the library so it reads  SYS/termcap as it stands.  The archive's build (gcc 1.4.2 and TOP  ncurses) sent every cursor move as ESC [ ; H -- the row and column were  empty -- so its whole display piled onto the top two lines; and it read  TERMCAP as the terminal description itself.  This build draws where it  should with TERMCAP naming the file, as SYS/login sets it.  hex.c: proto.h is only read by an ANSI compiler; for cc the same  functions are now declared without their prototypes, or cc stops on  `declaration mismatch' at each static void function.  Nothing else is  changed.  The original is hex.c.ori.